# OpenCode & Superpowers Installation

Install and configure the OpenCode.ai CLI tool and the Superpowers plugin on Windows.

## Proposed Changes

### System Environment
#### [MODIFY] PATH
- Add `C:\Users\Deacjx\AppData\Roaming\npm` to the User PATH to enable the `opencode` command.

### OpenCode Configuration
#### [NEW] [superpowers](file:///C:/Users/Deacjx/.config/opencode/superpowers)
- Clone the Superpowers repository: `git clone https://github.com/obra/superpowers.git "$env:USERPROFILE\.config\opencode\superpowers"`

#### [MODIFY] [superpowers.js](file:///C:/Users/Deacjx/.config/opencode/plugins/superpowers.js)
- Replace existing file with a Symbolic Link to `superpowers\.opencode\plugins\superpowers.js`.

#### [MODIFY] [superpowers](file:///C:/Users/Deacjx/.config/opencode/skills/superpowers)
- Replace existing directory with a Junction to `superpowers\skills`.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- Run `opencode --version` to verify command recognition.
- Run `Get-ChildItem "$env:USERPROFILE\.config\opencode\plugins" | Where-Object { $_.LinkType }` to verify symlink.
- Run `Get-ChildItem "$env:USERPROFILE\.config\opencode\skills" | Where-Object { $_.LinkType }` to verify junction.
- Check if `opencode` runs without errors in a new terminal session.
